1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:04,870
In the town there were two mutes, and they were always together.
镇上有两个哑巴，他们总是形影不离。

2
00:00:05,670 --> 00:00:11,570
Early every morning they would come out from the house where they lived and walk arm in arm down the street to work.
每天一大早，他们都会从住处出来，手挽着手沿街走去上班。

3
00:00:12,370 --> 00:00:15,930
The one who always steered the way was an obese and dreamy Greek.
总在前面领路的那个，是个肥胖而迷迷糊糊的希腊人。

4
00:00:16,730 --> 00:00:24,520
In the summer he would come out wearing a yellow or green polo shirt stuffed sloppily into his trousers in front and hanging loose behind.
夏天，他出门时会穿一件黄色或绿色的马球衫，前面胡乱塞在裤子里，后面松松垮垮地耷拉着。

5
00:00:25,320 --> 00:00:28,940
When it was colder, he wore over this a shapeless gray sweater.
天冷一些的时候，他就在外面套一件走了样的灰毛衣。

6
00:00:29,740 --> 00:00:35,900
His face was round and oily, with half-closed eyelids and lips that curved in a gentle, stupid smile.
他的脸圆圆的，油光光的，眼皮半闭着，嘴唇弯出一抹温和而傻乎乎的笑。

7
00:00:36,700 --> 00:00:38,170
The other mute was tall.
另一个哑巴个子很高。

8
00:00:38,970 --> 00:00:41,430
His eyes had a quick, intelligent expression.
他的眼睛透着机敏、聪慧的神情。

9
00:00:42,230 --> 00:00:45,240
He was always immaculate and very soberly dressed.
他总是收拾得一尘不染，穿着十分素净。

10
00:00:46,040 --> 00:00:51,300
Every morning the two friends walked silently together until they reached the main street of the town.
每天早上，这两个朋友都默默地一起走，一直走到镇上的大街。

11
00:00:52,100 --> 00:00:57,670
Then when they came to a certain fruit and candy store, they paused for a moment on the sidewalk outside.
接着，来到某家水果糖果店时，他们会在店外的人行道上停一会儿。

12
00:00:58,470 --> 00:01:04,100
The Greek, Spiros Antonapoulos, worked for his cousin, who owned this fruit store.
那个希腊人叫斯皮罗斯·安东尼帕罗斯，在他表兄手下干活，这家水果店就是表兄开的。

13
00:01:04,900 --> 00:01:09,670
His job was to make candies and sweets, uncrate the fruits, and keep the place clean.
他的活儿是做糖果和甜食，把水果从板条箱里取出来，还要保持店里干净。

14
00:01:10,470 --> 00:01:18,530
The thin mute, John Singer, nearly always put his hand on his friend’s arm and looked for a second into his face before leaving him.
那个瘦哑巴叫约翰·辛格，分开之前，他几乎每次都把手搭在朋友的胳膊上，注视他的脸片刻。

15
00:01:19,330 --> 00:01:26,670
Then after this goodbye Singer crossed the street and walked on alone to the jewelry store where he worked as a silverware engraver.
这样道别之后，辛格便穿过马路，独自继续往前走，一直走到那家珠宝店，他在那里当银器雕刻工。

16
00:01:27,470 --> 00:01:30,010
In the late afternoon the friends would meet again.
傍晚时分，两个朋友又会碰面。

17
00:01:30,810 --> 00:01:35,750
Singer came back to the fruit store and waited until Antonapoulos was ready to go home.
辛格回到水果店，一直等到安东尼帕罗斯准备好回家。

18
00:01:36,550 --> 00:01:44,690
The Greek would be lazily unpacking a case of peaches or melons, or perhaps looking at the funny paper in the kitchen behind the store where he cooked.
这时，那个希腊人往往正懒洋洋地拆一箱桃子或甜瓜，也可能正在店后面他做饭的厨房里看报上的连环漫画。

19
00:01:45,490 --> 00:01:52,500
Before their departure Antonapoulos always opened a paper sack he kept hidden during the day on one of the kitchen shelves.
临走前，安东尼帕罗斯总要打开一个纸袋，白天他一直把它藏在厨房的一层架子上。

20
00:01:53,300 --> 00:01:58,950
Inside were stored various bits of food he had collected—a piece of fruit or samples of candy.
袋子里存放着他攒下的各种零碎吃食——一个水果，或几块糖果样品。

21
00:01:59,750 --> 00:02:06,940
Usually before leaving Antonapoulos waddled gently to the glassed case in the front of the store where some meats and cheeses were kept.
离开前，安东尼帕罗斯通常会轻轻地、一摇一摆地走到店堂前部的玻璃柜跟前，柜子里放着一些肉和奶酪。

22
00:02:07,740 --> 00:02:14,930
He glided open the back of the case and his fat hand groped lovingly for some particular dainty inside which he had wanted.
他轻轻地滑开柜子背面的门，胖手满怀爱意地伸进去摸索，寻找他早就想要的某样精致小吃。

23
00:02:15,730 --> 00:02:18,880
Sometimes his cousin who owned the place did not see him.
有时候，开这家店的表兄没看见他。

24
00:02:19,680 --> 00:02:24,050
But if he noticed he stared at his cousin with a warning in his tight, pale face.
可要是表兄发现了，就会紧盯着这个表弟，紧绷而苍白的脸上带着警告的神色。

25
00:02:24,850 --> 00:02:29,690
Sadly, Antonapoulos would shuffle the morsel from one corner of the case to the other.
安东尼帕罗斯就会难过地把那一小块吃的从柜子的这一角挪到另一角。

26
00:02:30,490 --> 00:02:36,030
During these times Singer stood very straight with his hands in his pockets and looked in another direction.
每逢这种时候，辛格就把手插在口袋里，站得笔直，眼睛望向别处。

27
00:02:36,830 --> 00:02:40,130
He did not like to watch this little scene between the two Greeks.
他不喜欢看两个希腊人之间的这个小场面。

28
00:02:40,930 --> 00:02:48,060
For, except drinking and a certain solitary secret pleasure, Antonapoulos loved to eat more than anything else in the world.
因为，除了喝酒和某种独自享受的隐秘乐趣，安东尼帕罗斯在这世上最爱的就是吃。

29
00:02:48,860 --> 00:02:51,680
In the dusk the two mutes walked slowly home together.
暮色中，两个哑巴一起慢慢走回家。

30
00:02:52,480 --> 00:02:55,320
At home Singer was always talking to Antonapoulos.
在家里，辛格总是在跟安东尼帕罗斯说话。

31
00:02:56,120 --> 00:02:59,240
His hands shaped the words in a swift series of designs.
他的双手飞快地比画出一连串图形，打出一个个词。

32
00:03:00,040 --> 00:03:03,400
His face was eager and his gray-green eyes sparkled brightly.
他满脸热切，一双灰绿色的眼睛闪闪发亮。

33
00:03:04,200 --> 00:03:08,880
With his thin, strong hands he told Antonapoulos all that had happened during the day.
他用那双瘦削有力的手，把白天发生的一切都讲给安东尼帕罗斯听。

34
00:03:09,680 --> 00:03:13,890
When back at home, Antonapoulos sat back lazily and looked at Singer.
回到家里，安东尼帕罗斯便懒洋洋地往后一靠，看着辛格。

35
00:03:14,690 --> 00:03:21,840
It was seldom that he ever moved his hands to speak at all—and then it was to say that he wanted to eat or to sleep or to drink.
他难得动一动手来说话——即便动了，也只是说他想吃，或者想睡，或者想喝。

36
00:03:22,640 --> 00:03:26,510
These three things he always said with the same vague, fumbling signs.
这三件事，他总是用同样含糊、笨拙的手势来表示。

37
00:03:27,310 --> 00:03:32,750
At night, if he were not too drunk, he would kneel down before his bed and pray awhile.
夜里，要是醉得不太厉害，他会跪在床前祈祷一会儿。

38
00:03:33,550 --> 00:03:38,160
Then his plump hands shaped the words Holy Jesus, or God, or Darling Mary.
接着，他那双胖乎乎的手比画出“圣耶稣”，或“上帝”，或“亲爱的玛利亚”。

39
00:03:38,960 --> 00:03:41,830
These were the only words Antonapoulos ever said.
安东尼帕罗斯说过的词，就只有这几个。

40
00:03:42,630 --> 00:03:47,270
Singer never knew just how much his friend understood of all the things he told him.
辛格告诉朋友的种种事情，朋友究竟懂了多少，他从来都不知道。

41
00:03:48,070 --> 00:03:49,340
But it did not matter.
但这并不要紧。

42
00:03:50,140 --> 00:03:54,260
They shared the upstairs of a small house near the business section of the town.
他们合住在镇上商业区附近一座小房子的楼上。

43
00:03:55,060 --> 00:03:56,260
There were two rooms.
楼上共有两个房间。

44
00:03:57,060 --> 00:04:00,820
On the oil stove in the kitchen Antonapoulos cooked all of their meals.
他们的饭全是安东尼帕罗斯在厨房的油炉上做的。

45
00:04:01,620 --> 00:04:06,600
There were straight, plain kitchen chairs for Singer and an overstuffed sofa for Antonapoulos.
屋里给辛格准备的是几把直背的简朴厨房椅，给安东尼帕罗斯准备的是一张塞得鼓鼓囊囊的沙发。

46
00:04:07,400 --> 00:04:15,520
The bedroom was furnished mainly with a large double bed covered with an eiderdown comforter for the big Greek and a narrow iron cot for Singer.
卧室里主要摆着一张大双人床和一张窄窄的小铁床：双人床铺着鸭绒被，是给那个大块头希腊人睡的；小铁床是给辛格睡的。

47
00:04:16,320 --> 00:04:21,430
Dinner always took a long time, because Antonapoulos loved food and he was very slow.
晚饭总要吃很久，因为安东尼帕罗斯爱吃，吃得又非常慢。

48
00:04:22,230 --> 00:04:36,320
After they had eaten, the big Greek would lie back on his sofa and slowly lick over each one of his teeth with his tongue, either from a certain delicacy or because he did not wish to lose the savor of the meal—while Singer washed the dishes.
吃完饭，那个大块头希腊人会仰靠在沙发上，用舌头慢慢地把每一颗牙齿都舔一遍，要么是出于某种讲究，要么是因为不想让饭菜的余味散去；而辛格这时正在洗碗。

49
00:04:37,120 --> 00:04:39,750
Sometimes in the evening the mutes would play chess.
有时候晚上，两个哑巴会下国际象棋。

50
00:04:40,550 --> 00:04:46,270
Singer had always greatly enjoyed this game, and years before he had tried to teach it to Antonapoulos.
辛格一向非常喜爱这种棋，多年前就曾试着教安东尼帕罗斯下。

51
00:04:47,070 --> 00:04:52,860
At first his friend could not be interested in the reasons for moving the various pieces about on the board.
起初，他的朋友对棋盘上各种棋子为什么要那样挪来挪去，怎么也提不起兴趣。

52
00:04:53,660 --> 00:04:59,350
Then Singer began to keep a bottle of something good under the table to be taken out after each lesson.
后来，辛格开始在桌子底下放一瓶好东西，每上完一课就拿出来。

53
00:05:00,150 --> 00:05:08,750
The Greek never got on to the erratic movements of the knights and the sweeping mobility of the queens, but he learned to make a few set, opening moves.
那个希腊人始终没弄懂马那飘忽不定的走法和后那横扫全盘的机动性，不过他学会了几步固定的开局走法。

54
00:05:09,550 --> 00:05:13,630
He preferred the white pieces and would not play if the black men were given him.
他更喜欢执白棋，要是把黑子给他，他就不肯下。

55
00:05:14,430 --> 00:05:19,570
After the first moves Singer worked out the game by himself while his friend looked on drowsily.
走完开头几步后，辛格就自己把这盘棋下完，他的朋友则在一旁昏昏欲睡地看着。

56
00:05:20,370 --> 00:05:28,440
If Singer made brilliant attacks on his own men so that in the end the black king was killed, Antonapoulos was always very proud and pleased.
如果辛格对自己的棋子发起精彩的进攻，结果黑王最终被杀，安东尼帕罗斯总是非常得意、非常高兴。

57
00:05:29,240 --> 00:05:34,410
The two mutes had no other friends, and except when they worked, they were alone together.
两个哑巴没有别的朋友，除了上班的时候，总是只有他们俩待在一起。

58
00:05:35,210 --> 00:05:41,290
Each day was very much like any other day, because they were alone so much that nothing ever disturbed them.
每一天都和别的日子十分相像，因为两人独处得太多，从来没有什么事打扰过他们。

59
00:05:42,090 --> 00:05:48,610
Once a week they would go to the library for Singer to withdraw a mystery book and on Friday night they attended a movie.
他们每周去一次图书馆，好让辛格借一本推理小说；星期五晚上，他们会去看一场电影。

60
00:05:49,410 --> 00:05:57,550
Then on payday they always went to the ten-cent photograph shop above the Army and Navy Store so that Antonapoulos could have his picture taken.
此外，每逢发薪日，他们总要去陆海军商店楼上那家十美分一张的照相馆，好让安东尼帕罗斯拍张照片。

61
00:05:58,350 --> 00:06:01,650
These were the only places where they made customary visits.
他们惯常光顾的地方，就只有这几处。

62
00:06:02,450 --> 00:06:05,690
There were many parts in the town that they had never even seen.
镇上有许多地方，他们连见都没见过。

63
00:06:06,490 --> 00:06:08,680
The town was in the middle of the deep South.
这个镇子地处南方腹地的中部。

64
00:06:09,480 --> 00:06:13,250
The summers were long and the months of winter cold were very few.
这里夏季漫长，冬天寒冷的月份屈指可数。

65
00:06:14,050 --> 00:06:19,600
Nearly always the sky was a glassy, brilliant azure and the sun burned down riotously bright.
天空几乎总是玻璃般明净、灿烂夺目的蔚蓝色，太阳灼灼地照射下来，亮得放肆。

66
00:06:20,400 --> 00:06:27,370
Then the light, chill rains of November would come, and perhaps later there would be frost and some short months of cold.
然后，到了十一月，就会下起清冷的小雨，也许再往后会有霜冻，还有短短几个月的寒冷天气。

67
00:06:28,170 --> 00:06:32,110
The winters were changeable, but the summers always were burning hot.
这里的冬天变化无常，夏天却总是酷热难当。

68
00:06:32,910 --> 00:06:34,740
The town was a fairly large one.
这个镇子规模相当大。

69
00:06:35,540 --> 00:06:40,560
On the main street there were several blocks of two- and three-story shops and business offices.
大街上有好几个街区都是两三层的商店和商业办公楼。

70
00:06:41,360 --> 00:06:47,250
But the largest buildings in the town were the factories, which employed a large percentage of the population.
不过，镇上最大的建筑是工厂，这些工厂雇用了全镇很大一部分人口。

71
00:06:48,050 --> 00:06:53,140
These cotton mills were big and flourishing and most of the workers in the town were very poor.
这些棉纺厂规模庞大、生意兴隆，而镇上的大多数工人都非常贫穷。

72
00:06:53,940 --> 00:06:59,010
Often in the faces along the streets there was the desperate look of hunger and of loneliness.
街上的一张张面孔，常常流露出饥饿与孤独的绝望神情。

73
00:06:59,810 --> 00:07:01,930
But the two mutes were not lonely at all.
但这两个哑巴一点也不孤独。

74
00:07:02,730 --> 00:07:09,990
At home they were content to eat and drink, and Singer would talk with his hands eagerly to his friend about all that was in his mind.
在家里，他们吃吃喝喝就心满意足了；辛格会用双手热切地向朋友诉说心里想的一切。

75
00:07:10,790 --> 00:07:18,560
So, the years passed in this quiet way until Singer reached the age of thirty-two and had been in the town with Antonapoulos for ten years.
就这样，岁月平静地流逝，直到辛格到了三十二岁，已经和安东尼帕罗斯在这个镇上住了十年。
